AisenLens
=========

Copyright (c) 2026 AisenLens contributors.

The AisenShot scene-engine implementation in this repository is an
independent implementation. It does not copy source code from PySceneDetect,
OpenCut, OpenReel, or the previous AisenLens demo. Those projects were used
only for public design and data-model research as recorded in
reference-projects/REFERENCE_PROJECT_INDEX.md.

Third-party runtime and build dependencies are consumed through their package
or tool distributions and remain under their respective upstream licenses:

- React, React DOM, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, pnpm and related packages:
  see the package metadata and lockfile for the exact versions and licenses.
- Mediabunny: see the installed package license and upstream distribution.
- Emscripten SDK, LLVM-MinGW and CMake are build-time tools and are not
  redistributed in the AisenLens product bundle.

No test video, evaluation dataset, or local machine credential is included in
the product distribution. The four generated Scene Engine WASM runtime files
are intentionally versioned because they are required by the Web product;
local build caches and test artifacts remain excluded.
